      "notes": [
        "1. Install Ionizations device(s) whereindicated on drawings.",
        "2. Basis of Design: GPS Air. Substitutions must be approved by engineer, any mechanical or electrical modifications are the responsibility of the contractor.",
        "3. Ionizer has a self-cleaning feature to maintain ion output over 10 years, substitute products must document ionization output over time.",
        "4. Electronic air cleaners shall not have service parts, products that require replacement parts like glass tubes, UV lamps, catalysts, etc. are not acceptable.",
        "5. Must be listed to UL-2998 by either UL or ETL. Listing on UL and ETL website must include specific product family.",
        "6. Safety Tested by 3rd party laboratory to UL2998 Zero Ozone (ASHRAE Standard 241 Appendix A).",
        "7. Formaldehyde generation validated by 3rd party to ASTM D8407 emission rate less than 5μg/h (micro grams per hour) (ASHRAE Standard 241 Appendix A).",
        "8. Particle Generation validated by ISO14644 - results shall not exceed one cleanliness class greater than the empty chamber (ASHRAE Standard 241 Appendix A).",
        "9. Ion output is measured in ions per cubic centimeter (ions/cc) are verifiable with field instruments. Devices with ratings of ions/second are not acceptable.",
        "-- optional specifications --",
        "10. Powered by 277V, single phase, 60Hz via remote power supply.",
        "11. Powered by 347V, single phase, 60Hz via remote power supply."
      ]
