      "notes": [
        "1. Install Ionizations device(s) where indicated on drawings.",
        "2. Basis of Design: GPS Air. Substitutions must be approved by engineer, any mechanical or electrical modifications are the responsibility of the contractor.",
        "3. Ionizer has a self-cleaning feature to maintain ion output over 10 years, substitute products must document ionization output over time.",
        "4. Electronic air cleaners shall not have service parts, products that require replacement parts like glass tubes, UV lamps, catalysts, etc. are not acceptable.",
        "5. Must be listed to UL-2998 by either UL or ETL. Listing on UL and ETL website must include specific product family.",
        "6. Safety Tested by 3rd party laboratory to UL2998 Zero Ozone (ASHRAE Standard 241 Appendix A).",
        "7. Mount GPS-iMOD to air inlet side of cooling coil between 1/8\" and 1/2\" from grounded coil surface.",
        "8. Provide with integral BAS alarm contacts.",
        "9. Ionization bar to have a minimum of 1 needlepoint every 0.50\" of coil width. Systems with needles further apart shall not be acceptable (or shall require additional bars).",
        "10. Ionization systems with multiple ion modules mounted to a bar shall not be an acceptable substitute.",
        "11. Ionization output shall be a minimum of 70 million ions/cc for every 0.50\" of coil width.",
        "12. Ionization power supply shall have power on and plasma on indication light.",
        "13. Ionization bars shall be provided with magnets for ease of mounting.",
        "14. Ionization bars shall be modular and designed to cover the entire coil width in 6 inch increments.",
        "15. Provide stand-alone ion field detector to communicate with the BAS. (GPS-iDETECT-P Accessory)",
        "16. Must provide NEMA-4X rated enclosure for outdoor application.",
        "17. HCAI Seismic Compliance: Must be certified to HCAI Seismic Compliance standards."
      ]
