      "notes": [
        "1. Install Ionizations device(s) where indicated on drawings.",
        "2. Basis of Design: GPS Air. Substitutions must be approved by engineer, any mechanical or electrical modifications are the responsibility of the contractor.",
        "3. Ionizer has a self-cleaning feature to maintain ion output over 10 years, substitute products must document ionization output over time.",
        "4. Electronic filter enahncement systems shall not have service parts, products that require replacement parts like glass tubes, UV lamps, catalysts, etc. are not acceptable.",
        "5. Must be listed to UL-2998 by either UL or ETL. Listing on UL and ETL website must include specific product family.",
        "6. Provide with integral BAS alarm contacts.",
        "7. Mount GPS-Opti Lok 3 feet before the filter.",
        "8. Ion output is measured in ions per cubic centimeter (ions/cc) are verifiable with field instruments. Devices with ratings of ions/second are not acceptable.",
        "9. Provide integral BAS alarm contacts within the air cleaner."
      ]
    }
